From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiribbon: LoadUI finds the markup as a UIFILE resource

The Ribbon compiler's .rc embeds the compiled markup as resource type UIFILE; LoadUI looked for
UIRIBBON, so a real program's ribbon was "Resource type not found" (TreeSize Free 4.8 stopped at
TUIRibbon.Load). fastb-ribbon-gate.sh embeds UIFILE now.
---
--- a/dlls/uiribbon/uiribbon.c
+++ b/dlls/uiribbon/uiribbon.c
@@ -341,8 +341,14 @@
     LeaveCriticalSection(&This->cs);
     if (!app) return E_UNEXPECTED;
 
-    /* the compiled markup is a resource of type UIRIBBON */
+    /* the compiled markup is a resource of type UIFILE, as the Ribbon
+     * compiler's .rc names it (Stained Glass OS 9303: it was looked for as
+     * UIRIBBON, and TreeSize's ribbon "MAIN" was "Resource type not found") */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_RIBBON_WRONG_TYPE
+    res = FindResourceW(instance, resourceName, L"UIFILE");
+#else
     res = FindResourceW(instance, resourceName, L"UIRIBBON");
+#endif
     if (!res) return HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(GetLastError());
     if (!LoadResource(instance, res)) return HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(GetLastError());
 
